        "original_id": "c3ddb506-9008-5614-a7d0-6af0b8a89dd0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robbin Crosby\n- Organizations: Ratt, RIAA\n- Concepts: glam metal, heavy metal, Los Angeles glam metal scene, hair metal, pop metal\n\nFacts:\n- Robbinson Lantz Crosby was born on August 4, 1959, and died on June 6, 2002.\n- Robbin Crosby was an American guitarist and a member of the glam metal band Ratt.\n- In the 1980s, Ratt achieved significant commercial success in the United States.\n- In the 1980s, Robbin Crosby earned several platinum albums in the United States with Ratt.\n- Ratt's albums were certified gold, platinum, and multi-platinum by the RIAA.\n- In the early 1980s, Ratt and Mötley Crüe were recognized as instrumental in forming the Los Angeles glam metal scene.\n- The Los Angeles glam metal scene was also known as hair metal or pop metal.",
